$\text{ Hints: } \beta=50 \Rightarrow \beta=\frac{\Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{C}}}{\Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{B}}} \Rightarrow \Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{C}}=\beta \times \Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{B}}

\begin{aligned}& \Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{B}}=\frac{0.01}{10^3}=10^{-2} \times10^{-3}=10^{-5} \\
& \Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{C}}=50 \times10^{-5}=500 \times10^{-6}=500 \mu \mathrm{A}
\end{aligned}$

In given circuit, $V_{C C}=i_B R_B+V_{B E}
\Rightarrow \quad R_B=R_1=\frac{V_{C C}-V_{B E}}{i_B}$ As, $i_B=\frac{i_C}{\beta}=\frac{5 \times 10^{-3}}{50}=1 \times 10^{-4} \mathrm{ A}
\Rightarrow \quad R_1=\frac{8-0.6}{1 \times 10-4}=7.4 \times10^4=74 \times10^3 \Omega=74 \mathrm{k} \Omega and $by KVL in closed collector loop, we get \Rightarrow \quad$\begin{aligned} V_{C C} \text{ and } =i_C R_L+V_{C E} \\
R_L \text{ and } =\frac{V_{C C}-V_{C E}}{i_C}\\ \text{ and } =\frac{8-3}{5 \times 10^{-3}}
\end{aligned}$ So, R_2=R_L=1.0 $\mathrm{k} \Omega$
